+### Test counts
+
+Two counts appear in this document and only one of them arrives with a command.
+
+The author runs `npm test` in the verifier folder at `05267a36` and reports 36 tests across 3 files. That is the count to quote, because the tree and the command travel with it.
+
+The 29 of 29 that stood in every earlier revision is withdrawn. It carried no command and no file list, and I cannot re-derive it: the verifier is not in my working copy, so there is no run of mine behind it that I can point at. The same goes for the pass and fail pair once reported in W-02's ordering hazard, which was an observation on a throwaway patch and never a suite count.
+
+The likely explanation is that `05267a36` carries tests added after `b890d2c`, spread over two more files. I have not checked that, and I will not record it as a finding until I have. What the register can say now is what each number is attached to, and the honest answer for one of them is nothing.
+
 Both output files and the patch itself are kept with the review rather than pasted into this document, so that the figures above can be re-derived without trusting the transcription.
